# BUILDFLOW — PROJECT MANAGER DASHBOARD
## Complete UI/UX and Functional Development Prompt

Build a premium, enterprise-grade **Project Manager Dashboard** for BuildFlow, a multi-tenant Construction Workforce Management and Project Operations SaaS platform.

Build this dashboard completely from scratch. Do not reuse the existing Company Admin or Site Manager dashboard layouts. Create a dedicated Project Manager experience with its own information architecture, navigation, project-focused workflows, analytics and responsive interface.

This is a real construction project management workspace, not a generic admin dashboard or static analytics template.

---

# 1. PROJECT MANAGER — ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES

The Project Manager oversees multiple projects and their associated construction sites.

Their responsibilities include:

- Monitoring progress across all assigned projects.
- Comparing the performance of different construction sites.
- Tracking project budgets, expenses and financial forecasts.
- Monitoring workforce strength and labour deployment.
- Tracking project milestones and deadlines.
- Monitoring site managers, engineers and supervisors.
- Reviewing daily progress reports.
- Identifying delayed activities and project risks.
- Reviewing material and equipment availability.
- Monitoring project-level purchase requests.
- Reviewing project-level expenses within authorized limits.
- Escalating operational issues to Company Admin.
- Preparing project performance reports.
- Ensuring projects are completed within approved budgets and timelines.

IMPORTANT ROLE RULE:

A Project Manager should only access projects explicitly assigned to them.

They should not automatically receive access to every company project, employee salary record, company-wide finance records or unrestricted HR administration.

Permissions must be configurable by the Company Admin.

A Project Manager may oversee several projects, and each project may have several sites, Site Managers, Site Engineers and Supervisors.

