# 23. IMPORTANT BUSINESS LOGIC

Implement the following rules:

1. A Project Manager sees only assigned projects.
2. Project data must never leak across organizations.
3. Project progress must be calculated using defined milestone or work-quantity rules, not random percentages.
4. Planned and actual progress must be displayed separately.
5. Original project deadlines must be preserved when dates are revised.
6. Budget, committed cost, approved expenditure and paid expenditure must remain separate.
7. Pending expenses must not be shown as paid expenses.
8. Workforce totals must be based on valid project assignments.
9. Attendance information must respect the selected reporting date and timezone.
10. Historical project assignments must be preserved for accurate reporting.
11. Critical issues must be escalated through the configured workflow.
12. Approvals must be permission-controlled and auditable.
13. Project Managers cannot directly modify payroll or confidential employee salary records without explicit authorization.
14. Document access must be permission-controlled.
15. Every important update must have an audit history.
16. Project health indicators must have transparent explanations.
17. Missing data must be shown as unavailable, not silently treated as zero.
18. All currency values must use decimal-safe calculations and display in INR.
19. Do not hardcode legal or financial thresholds.
20. Do not claim that location, attendance, material or financial data is live unless it is actually connected and verified.

